abstract: "## SoilHarmony, Work Package 5\n\nDeliverable D5.1 – Statistical analysis
  plan for best practices for the development and validation of TF and PTF.\n\nFrom
  the grant agreement, Annex 1, part B:\n\nAs a first step, WP5 will develop a statistical
  analysis plan based on input from WP1, i.e., determining statistical practices in
  use regarding TF and PTF (supply-side analysis) and the requirements of the call
  and the SML (demand-side analysis). For the supply-side analysis, partners will
  determine which information needs to be extracted from published sources related
  to TF/PTF to make a statistical assessment of their quality and applicability. This
  will include, a.o., algorithm used, required input data, characteristics of the
  training data, uncertainty of the estimation, type of validation (non, cross-validation,
  or independent validation set). The various statistical methods will then be first
  divided into methods related to method comparison; methods associated with TF development
  and methods related to PTF development. Their underlying assumptions will be made
  explicit, and conceptually similar models/methods will be grouped. For instance,
  within TF models, a distinction will be made between asymmetrical (e.g. linear regression
  models) and symmetrical models (e.g. orthogonal or major axis regression, Deming
  regression, ...). Relevant literature on similar statistical techniques will also
  be drawn from other scientific domains. For the demand-side analysis, partners will
  translate the requirements of the call and SML to clearly defined research questions
  to which a specific statistical task can be attributed. The demand and supply sides
  will then be confronted with each other and synthesized, resulting in a list of
  methods suitable for answering the various research questions and statistical tasks.
  Potential knowledge gaps regarding statistical methods will be identified. Each
  of the research questions will naturally depend on the others, reflecting the TF
  and PTF life cycle (development, validation, use), which will form the basis of
  the statistical analysis plan. Best statistical practices will be identified and
  applied in the statistical analysis plan, which forms the backbone of WP5 tasks.\n\nThis
  github repo will be used for writing the statistical analysis plan.\n"
version: 0.0.0
